findings:
Tests (tests/test_github_read_request_v5.py) are meaningful and use literal expectations, not recomputed quote() results. They cover:
- exact issue and file argv tuples and defaults;
- the scope's Unicode/space/$/;/#/? encoding literal, plus '%' to %25, nested paths and +&=;
- FrozenInstanceError on every field, argv as a tuple of str, and caller-side mutation of the input dict after the call;
- bad capability values, crossed keys, a dict subclass, non-str keys, bool/float/str/huge numbers including 10**5000;
- denied repository variants, and all listed path escape/control/surrogate cases;
- uppercase, short, long, branch-name and non-str refs;
- both bounds with 1/max accepted, max+1 as limit, and 0/negative/bool/float as invalid_input;
- ordering, and sentinel no-echo checks on str, repr, message and args.
The _error helper asserts __cause__/__context__ None and args == (message,) for every rejection. Small gaps: there is no str-subclass-key case, and no test asserts C1 or bidi characters are accepted, although the design allows them.
